DSLean
------
Source:   https://github.com/taterowney/DSLean; SymLean requires the Lean 4.35.0 port
          https://github.com/Robertboy18/DSLean, branch leancas, revision 1b5f22f
Author:   taterowney (GitHub) and the DSLean contributors
License:  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
          https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
          DSLean is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind; see Section 5 of that
          license.

The optional oracle library of SymLean (CASOracle/) depends on DSLean, which SymLean fetches only
with `lake -R -Koracle=on`. DSLean's grammars translate between Lean and the languages of the
oracles, and its runner runs them. The branch leancas is DSLean's update to Lean 4.35.0 with five
changes: operand precedences that follow the precedence option, pattern priorities that hold in
toExternal', a runner with a deadline and a bounded output (DSLean/Process.lean), Gappa's input
grammar in a module of its own, and info trees turned off while the gappa tactic elaborates the
proof it generates. No DSLean file is copied into SymLean.

Hex
---
Source:   https://github.com/leanprover/hex (v0.10.0)
Author:   the Lean FRO and the Hex contributors
License:  Apache License 2.0

The optional routes of CASHex/ use Hex's libraries, which SymLean fetches only with
`lake -R -Khex=on update`. The file in CASHex/patches is a modification of a Hex source file
(HexLLL) that lets it build on glibc systems with this toolchain; it is applied by hand to the
fetched package, as Site/Pages/guide/hex.md describes.

